WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.790
This is the Singularity Daily, for Thursday, November 19.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.300
Let's catch you up on the last 24 hours in superintelligence.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.420
Records fell today.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:21.880
Anthropic priced its stock market debut at $83 a share, above its range.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.860
That values the maker of Claude at about $1.5 trillion.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.880
It raised over $81 billion,

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:38.190
the biggest stock market debut on record, beating SpaceX.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:43.410
Its boss, Dario Amodei, told investors that done right,

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.900
AI can create an age of miracles.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:53.070
Meanwhile, Nvidia's sales more than doubled in a year, to nearly $116 billion.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:56.230
Its board says Jensen Huang isn't coming back,

00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:58.840
and the interim boss says: we've got this.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.940
Google launched Gemini 4 Neon, an AI model built for real work,

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:06.260
from spreadsheets to legal research.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.410
In a simulated vending machine business,

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:14.190
it made nearly $17,000, the top score, Google says.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.890
And Nvidia has stopped shipping its powerful Hopper chips to China,

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:20.220
even with US approval.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.280
Sam Altman,

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:28.640
on the idea of humans as AI's happy pets: "I don't want to be a Labrador."

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.240
Researchers used AI to find a critical flaw in Java,

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:35.490
the code most big companies run on.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:42.510
It took one hour and under $200 of AI time. A fix is already out.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:45.670
The catch?

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:51.390
Government testers got four top chatbots to help plan terror attacks within 12 hours.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:53.930
Waymo pulled its robotaxis off US freewa

00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:56.360
ys after California called them a hazard.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:07.460
Robots broke a record too. 151 danced in sync in Shenzhen, China.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:13.050
The show welcomed world leaders to a big Asia-Pacific summit there.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:20.660
And India's Humyn Labs raised $47 million to film everyday tasks,

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:22.540
so robots can learn them.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:26.950
Records fall every day now. Let's make sure people rise with them.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.030
Day after day, the curve keeps bending upward.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.970
Every day, the future shows up a little earlier.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.930
All of that, in one day. And the days keep getting bigger.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.100
This has been the Singularity Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.340
Go build something. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.010
Want the whole month? Hear more on November 27.
